# Trancendos worker base image — carries the Shared Functional Services Core
# into every own-context worker.
#
# THE PROBLEM
#
# 74 of 174 compose services build from their own directory, so nothing at the
# repo root is in their images. `Dimensional/` (the SFSC) and
# `src/observability/` are therefore unreachable to them. The consequences are
# measured, not theoretical:
#
#   * `instrument_worker` is imported by 34 workers and runs in none of them —
#     Prometheus metrics and OTel tracing are silently absent platform-wide,
#     while CLAUDE.md claims "W3C TraceContext propagation across all workers".
#   * 41 services hand-rolled their own X-Internal-Secret check because they
#     could not import a shared one. Four of those failed open and 18 compared
#     with `!=`.
#   * chaos-party wrote an eighth circuit breaker after an ADR consolidated the
#     other seven onto a home it could not reach.
#
# WHY A BASE IMAGE AND NOT THE ALTERNATIVES
#
#   Vendoring (copy the files into each build context) works — hive-service and
#   dimensional-nexus-service already do it — but it means ~41 duplicated
#   subtrees in git, each needing a "keep in sync" promise. That promise is now
#   machine-checked (scripts/check_worker_build_context.py), which makes
#   vendoring safe, not cheap.
#
#   Packaging as a wheel does not actually solve it. A local wheel still has to
#   be *inside* the build context to be installed, so it lands back on the same
#   reachability problem with an extra build step attached.
#
#   Compose named contexts (`additional_contexts:`) are elegant and this
#   Compose version accepts them — but `.forgejo/workflows/deploy-self-hosted.yml`
#   builds with plain `docker build -t X workers/X/`, not `docker compose build`,
#   so a compose-only feature would be ignored by the pipeline that actually
#   produces production images.
#
#   A base image works with plain `docker build`, needs no per-service file
#   copies, and cannot drift because there is exactly one copy. 37 of the 41
#   services that need the core already share the identical pinned base below,
#   so for them this is a one-line FROM change.
#
# WHERE IT LIVES
#
# The platform already runs a Zot OCI registry as The Artifactory
# (`zot:5000`, docker-compose.production.yml), described in that file as
# "All workers can pull images from http://zot:5000 inside the network." That
# is the natural home — self-hosted, zero-cost, already deployed. No new
# infrastructure, no external registry, consistent with architecture principle
# 4 (self-hosted over vendor services).
#
# BUILD
#   docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.worker-base -t zot:5000/trancendos-worker-base:3.11 .
# The build context is the REPO ROOT, because that is where the core lives.
#
# NOTE ON THE 4 SERVICES THIS DOES NOT COVER
# artifactory-service, imaginarium and two others build on python:3.12-slim.
# They need a 3.12 tag of this same file (change the FROM, nothing else) or stay
# vendored. Deliberately not papered over: one base image does not silently
# become correct for a different Python minor version.

FROM python:3.11-slim@sha256:e031123e3d85762b141ad1cbc56452ba69c6e722ebf2f042cc0dc86c47c0d8b3

# Non-root by default, matching every worker Dockerfile in the estate so a
# derived image does not have to re-create the user.
RUN groupadd -r worker && useradd -r -g worker -d /app -s /sbin/nologin worker

WORKDIR /app

# The shared core. Copied as two explicit trees rather than the whole repo:
# a base image that carried all of src/ would drag the FastAPI app, the model
# code and the test suite into 37 worker images for the sake of two packages.
COPY --chown=worker:worker Dimensional/ /app/Dimensional/
COPY --chown=worker:worker src/__init__.py /app/src/__init__.py
COPY --chown=worker:worker src/observability/ /app/src/observability/

# `src/observability/worker_setup.py` degrades to a no-op when its optional
# packages are absent, so they are NOT installed here — a worker that wants
# real telemetry adds them to its own requirements. This keeps the base small
# and keeps the choice with the service.

# PYTHONPATH so a derived image's `from Dimensional...` and
# `from src.observability...` resolve regardless of that worker's WORKDIR.
ENV PYTHONPATH=/app

# Derived images set their own USER, CMD and healthcheck. This one is a base:
# it deliberately has no entrypoint, so `docker run` on it does nothing useful
# and cannot be mistaken for a service.
